Subject: [PATCH] Refactor test IDE bundled plugin classpath to preserve classloader isolation

Rewrite BundledPluginsPathArgumentProvider to pass all shared plugins  
via `plugin.path` with explicit `idea.load.plugins.id` selection instead  
of relying on version-gated classpath flattening. The new approach  
resolves plugin IDs from sandbox, shared classpath JARs, and bundled  
plugin directories, then constrains loading to only those IDs plus the  
core IntelliJ module.

Key changes:
- Replace version-based classpath switching with unified plugin.path
  argument generation in BundledPluginsPathArgumentProvider
- Add shared classpath and sandbox plugins directory inputs to the
  argument provider for accurate plugin ID resolution
- Extract test framework runtime (idea_rt.jar) separately without
  pulling in its owning Java or JUnit plugins
- Filter isolated bundled plugin discovery using
  TestIdeBundledPluginsClasspathExcludes property
- Update integration tests to verify isolation across multiple IDE
  versions and configuration-cache reuse
- Add tests for distribution metadata retention, framework runtime
  loading, and Git extension compatibility without conflicting modules
